<%!-- Automatic post deletion (issue #1255): the member's own rule for letting
their posts age out. Off for everybody until they switch it on, and every
exception defaults to keeping more, so a member who ticks the switch without
reading the page loses the least.

Three things this page has to say plainly, in this order: what it deletes, that
deletion cannot be undone, and that a copy on another server is a request we
send and not a switch we hold. The last one gets its own explainer card rather
than a line of small print — a member who federates is publishing to servers
this installation does not run, and that is exactly the expectation this
feature could otherwise create falsely.

The confirmation dialog at the bottom renders only while @confirm is set (the
controller's step 1). It is a server-rendered panel, not a JS modal: this is a
classic controller page, the whole flow is two POSTs, and a confirmation that
depends on JavaScript is the wrong place to start relying on it. --%>
<.settings_shell
  user={@user}
  active={:auto_post_deletion}
  title={gettext("Automatic post deletion")}
>
  <div class="space-y-6">
    <.card>
      <.section_title>{gettext("What this does")}</.section_title>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        {gettext(
          "With this on, your own posts are deleted once they pass the age you pick. It runs once a day and only ever touches your posts, never anyone else's."
        )}
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        {gettext(
          "Deleting a post cannot be undone. Your pinned post and any post a moderator is currently looking at are always kept."
        )}
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        {gettext("You can download everything you have here first:")}
        <.link
          navigate={~p"/#{@user.username}/export"}
          class="font-semibold text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-700 dark:text-brand-400 dark:hover:text-brand-300"
        >
          {gettext("Download your data")}
        </.link>
      </p>
    </.card>

    <%!-- The Fediverse half, stated as what it is: a request. Rendered for
          everyone rather than only for federating members, because a member
          who has never federated may well switch it on later, and finding out
          then that "delete" meant something weaker would be the wrong moment
          to learn it. --%>
    <.card>
      <.section_title>{gettext("What we cannot promise")}</.section_title>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        {gettext(
          "If a post of yours reached other networks (Mastodon and the rest), we ask every server that received it to delete its copy. We cannot make them. A server that is switched off, that no longer talks to us, or that simply ignores the request keeps what it has."
        )}
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        {gettext(
          "Copies people made themselves are out of reach entirely: a screenshot, a quote, a search engine's cache. Deleting a post here removes it from vutuv; it does not recall it from the internet."
        )}
      </p>
    </.card>

    <.card>
      <.section_title>{gettext("Your rule")}</.section_title>

      <.form
        :let={f}
        for={@changeset}
        action={~p"/settings/auto_post_deletion"}
        id="auto-post-deletion-form"
        class="mt-5 space-y-6"
      >
        <.form_error changeset={@changeset} />

        <.setting_toggle label={gettext("Delete my posts automatically")}>
          <:checkbox><%= checkbox f, :auto_post_deletion?, class: checkbox_class() %></:checkbox>
          {gettext("Off by default. Nothing is deleted until you switch this on and save.")}
        </.setting_toggle>

        <div>
          <label
            for={input_id(f, :auto_post_deletion_after_days)}
            class="block text-sm font-medium text-slate-900 dark:text-white"
          >
            {gettext("Delete posts older than")}
          </label>
          <%= select f, :auto_post_deletion_after_days, auto_post_deletion_options(),
                prompt: gettext("Please choose"),
                class: [input_class(f, :auto_post_deletion_after_days), "mt-1 max-w-xs"] %>
          <%= error_tag f, :auto_post_deletion_after_days %>
          <p
            :if={!f.errors[:auto_post_deletion_after_days]}
            class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400"
          >
            {gettext("Counted from when you posted it.")}
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-4 border-t border-slate-100 pt-5 dark:border-slate-800">
          <p class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            {gettext("Always keep")}
          </p>

          <.setting_toggle label={gettext("Posts with photos or a review")}>
            <:checkbox>
              <%= checkbox f, :auto_post_deletion_keep_photos?, class: checkbox_class() %>
            </:checkbox>
            {gettext("Photo posts and book or film reviews are kept whatever their age.")}
          </.setting_toggle>

          <.setting_toggle label={gettext("Posts somebody answered")}>
            <:checkbox>
              <%= checkbox f, :auto_post_deletion_keep_answered?, class: checkbox_class() %>
            </:checkbox>
            {gettext("Deleting a post that started a conversation leaves the replies without their beginning.")}
          </.setting_toggle>

          <.setting_toggle label={gettext("Posts you bookmarked yourself")}>
            <:checkbox>
              <%= checkbox f, :auto_post_deletion_keep_bookmarked?, class: checkbox_class() %>
            </:checkbox>
            {gettext("Bookmark one of your own posts and this rule steps over it. That is how you keep a single post.")}
          </.setting_toggle>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-4 border-t border-slate-100 pt-5 dark:border-slate-800">
          <p class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            {gettext("Also delete")}
          </p>

          <.setting_toggle label={gettext("My replies in other people's threads")}>
            <:checkbox>
              <%= checkbox f, :auto_post_deletion_delete_replies?, class: checkbox_class() %>
            </:checkbox>
            {gettext("Off by default: a reply is one turn in a conversation that is not only yours.")}
          </.setting_toggle>
        </div>

        <%!-- The engagement floors. 0 = off, which is why each hint says so
              rather than leaving an empty-looking number field to be guessed
              at. Likes and reposts count what other networks did too, because
              that is the figure the member is shown on their own post. --%>
        <div class="space-y-4 border-t border-slate-100 pt-5 dark:border-slate-800">
          <p class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            {gettext("Keep posts that did well")}
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            {gettext("A post that reached one of these numbers is kept. Leave a field at 0 to switch it off. Likes and reposts include the ones from other networks, the same numbers you see on the post itself.")}
          </p>

          <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
            <div>
              <label
                for={input_id(f, :auto_post_deletion_min_likes)}
                class="block text-sm font-medium text-slate-900 dark:text-white"
              >
                {gettext("Likes")}
              </label>
              <%= number_input f, :auto_post_deletion_min_likes,
                    min: 0,
                    class: [input_class(f, :auto_post_deletion_min_likes), "mt-1"] %>
              <%= error_tag f, :auto_post_deletion_min_likes %>
            </div>

            <div>
              <label
                for={input_id(f, :auto_post_deletion_min_bookmarks)}
                class="block text-sm font-medium text-slate-900 dark:text-white"
              >
                {gettext("Bookmarks")}
              </label>
              <%= number_input f, :auto_post_deletion_min_bookmarks,
                    min: 0,
                    class: [input_class(f, :auto_post_deletion_min_bookmarks), "mt-1"] %>
              <%= error_tag f, :auto_post_deletion_min_bookmarks %>
            </div>

            <div>
              <label
                for={input_id(f, :auto_post_deletion_min_reposts)}
                class="block text-sm font-medium text-slate-900 dark:text-white"
              >
                {gettext("Reposts")}
              </label>
              <%= number_input f, :auto_post_deletion_min_reposts,
                    min: 0,
                    class: [input_class(f, :auto_post_deletion_min_reposts), "mt-1"] %>
              <%= error_tag f, :auto_post_deletion_min_reposts %>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="border-t border-slate-100 pt-5 dark:border-slate-800">
          <.button type="submit">{gettext("Save")}</.button>
        </div>
      </.form>
    </.card>

    <%!-- What the rule as SAVED would take on the next pass. Shown only while
          the rule is on and has something to take, so the page is quiet for
          everyone else. --%>
    <p
      :if={@due_count > 0 and is_nil(@confirm)}
      id="auto-post-deletion-due"
      data-due-count={@due_count}
      class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400"
    >
      {ngettext(
        "%{count} of your posts is currently past this age.",
        "%{formatted} of your posts are currently past this age.",
        @due_count,
        formatted: delimited_count(@due_count)
      )}
    </p>
  </div>

  <%!-- The confirmation. It names the exact number the rule would take right
        now (counted with the same query the sweeper deletes by), carries the
        submitted values back untouched as hidden fields, and repeats the two
        things that cannot be taken back: the deletion itself, and the copies
        on servers we do not run. --%>
  <div
    :if={@confirm}
    id="auto-post-deletion-confirm"
    class="fixed inset-0 z-50 flex items-end justify-center bg-slate-900/60 p-4 sm:items-center"
    role="dialog"
    aria-modal="true"
    aria-labelledby="auto-post-deletion-confirm-title"
  >
    <div class="w-full max-w-lg rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 shadow-lg ring-1 ring-slate-200 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:ring-slate-800">
      <h2
        id="auto-post-deletion-confirm-title"
        class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white"
      >
        {ngettext(
          "Delete %{count} post now?",
          "Delete %{formatted} posts now?",
          @confirm.count,
          formatted: delimited_count(@confirm.count)
        )}
      </h2>

      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        {ngettext(
          "Saving this rule deletes %{count} post straight away. It cannot be undone.",
          "Saving this rule deletes %{formatted} posts straight away. This cannot be undone.",
          @confirm.count,
          formatted: delimited_count(@confirm.count)
        )}
      </p>

      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        {gettext("We will ask other networks to delete their copies as well, but we cannot make them.")}
      </p>

      <.form
        for={@changeset}
        action={~p"/settings/auto_post_deletion"}
        id="auto-post-deletion-confirm-form"
        class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3"
      >
        <%= for {field, value} <- @confirm.params, field != "confirmed" do %>
          <input type="hidden" name={"user[#{field}]"} value={value} />
        <% end %>
        <input type="hidden" name="user[confirmed]" value="true" />

        <.button type="submit" variant="danger" id="auto-post-deletion-confirm-submit">
          {gettext("Delete and save")}
        </.button>
        <.link
          navigate={~p"/settings/auto_post_deletion"}
          class="text-sm font-semibold text-slate-600 hover:text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-400 dark:hover:text-slate-200"
        >
          {gettext("Cancel")}
        </.link>
      </.form>
    </div>
  </div>
</.settings_shell>
